WEBVTT

00:00.003 --> 00:01.043
- [Instructor] This right over here

00:01.043 --> 00:04.607
is the graph of y is equal
to absolute value of x

00:04.607 --> 00:06.037
which you might be familiar with.

00:06.037 --> 00:08.213
If you take x is equal to negative two,

00:08.213 --> 00:11.431
the absolute value of
that is going to be two.

00:11.431 --> 00:13.473
Negative one, absolute value is one.

00:13.473 --> 00:15.308
Zero, absolute value is zero.

00:15.308 --> 00:17.735
One, absolute value is one.

00:17.735 --> 00:19.514
So on and so forth.

00:19.514 --> 00:20.786
What I wanna do in this video

00:20.786 --> 00:23.992
is think about how the
equation will change

00:23.992 --> 00:26.327
if we were to shift this graph.

00:26.327 --> 00:28.457
So in particular, we're
gonna first think about

00:28.457 --> 00:32.624
what would be the equation
of this graph if we shift,

00:33.633 --> 00:36.133
if we shift three to the right

00:38.132 --> 00:41.034
and then think about how that will change

00:41.034 --> 00:43.038
if not only do we shift three to the right

00:43.038 --> 00:45.205
but we also shift four up,

00:46.869 --> 00:48.036
shift four up,

00:49.855 --> 00:53.617
and so once again pause this
video like we always say

00:53.617 --> 00:55.785
and figure out what would the equation be

00:55.785 --> 00:59.674
if you shift three to
the right and four up?

00:59.674 --> 01:01.347
Alright, now let's do this together.

01:01.347 --> 01:03.512
So let's just first
shift three to the right

01:03.512 --> 01:06.339
and think about how that
might change the equation.

01:06.339 --> 01:10.955
So let's just visualize what
we're even talking about.

01:10.955 --> 01:14.255
So if we're gonna shift
three to the right,

01:14.255 --> 01:16.290
it would look like,

01:16.290 --> 01:18.781
it would look like this.

01:18.781 --> 01:22.948
So that's what we first wanna
figure out the equation for

01:24.396 --> 01:27.636
and so how would we think about it?

01:27.636 --> 01:29.812
Well, one way to think about it is,

01:29.812 --> 01:31.783
well, something interesting is happening

01:31.783 --> 01:34.275
right over here at x equals three.

01:34.275 --> 01:36.317
Before, that interesting
thing was happening

01:36.317 --> 01:37.819
at x equals zero.

01:37.819 --> 01:40.168
Now, it's happening at x equals three.

01:40.168 --> 01:41.928
And the interesting
thing that happens here

01:41.928 --> 01:45.279
is that you switch signs
inside the absolute value.

01:45.279 --> 01:47.818
Instead of taking an
absolute value of a negative,

01:47.818 --> 01:49.454
you're now taking the absolute value

01:49.454 --> 01:52.191
as you cross this point of a positive

01:52.191 --> 01:55.507
and that's why we see a
switch in direction here

01:55.507 --> 01:56.507
of this line

01:57.591 --> 02:00.576
and so you see the same thing
happening right over here.

02:00.576 --> 02:03.326
So at this point right over here,

02:04.412 --> 02:07.105
we know that our function,

02:07.105 --> 02:11.560
we know that our equation
needs to evaluate out to zero

02:11.560 --> 02:15.227
and this is where it's
going to switch signs

02:16.330 --> 02:19.235
and so we say, okay, well, this
looks like an absolute value

02:19.235 --> 02:20.750
so it's going to have the form,

02:20.750 --> 02:25.330
y is equal to the absolute
value of something

02:25.330 --> 02:28.109
and so you say, okay, if x is three,

02:28.109 --> 02:31.265
how do I make that equal to zero?

02:31.265 --> 02:34.571
Well, I can subtract three from it.

02:34.571 --> 02:38.738
If I say y is equal to the
absolute value of x minus three,

02:39.761 --> 02:40.623
well, let's try it out.

02:40.623 --> 02:42.426
Let's see if it makes sense.

02:42.426 --> 02:44.597
So when x is equal to three,

02:44.597 --> 02:46.316
three minus three is zero,

02:46.316 --> 02:47.666
absolute value of that is zero.

02:47.666 --> 02:48.853
That works out.

02:48.853 --> 02:50.445
When x is equal to four,

02:50.445 --> 02:54.612
four minus three is one,
absolute value of one is indeed,

02:55.794 --> 02:56.961
is indeed one.

02:58.000 --> 02:59.962
And if x is equal to two,

02:59.962 --> 03:02.215
well, two minus three is negative one

03:02.215 --> 03:04.791
but the absolute value of that is one.

03:04.791 --> 03:06.586
So once again, I'm showing you this

03:06.586 --> 03:08.011
by really trying out numbers,

03:08.011 --> 03:09.793
trying to give you a
little bit of an intuition

03:09.793 --> 03:12.422
because that wasn't obvious to
me when I first learned this

03:12.422 --> 03:14.914
that if I'm shifting to the right

03:14.914 --> 03:17.528
which it looks like I'm
increasing an x value

03:17.528 --> 03:20.516
but what I would really do is replace my x

03:20.516 --> 03:24.520
with an x minus the amount
that I'm shifting to the right

03:24.520 --> 03:26.072
but I encourage you to try numbers

03:26.072 --> 03:28.086
and think about what's happening here.

03:28.086 --> 03:30.669
At this vertex right over here,

03:32.447 --> 03:36.737
whatever was in the absolute
value sign was equaling zero.

03:36.737 --> 03:38.660
It's when whatever was in
the absolute value sign

03:38.660 --> 03:41.851
is switching from negative
signs to positive signs.

03:41.851 --> 03:45.165
So once again, if you
shift three to the right,

03:45.165 --> 03:47.899
that has to happen at x equals three.

03:47.899 --> 03:51.332
So whatever is inside
the absolute value sign

03:51.332 --> 03:55.263
has to be equal to zero at
x equals three and this,

03:55.263 --> 03:57.050
pause this video and
really think about this

03:57.050 --> 03:58.569
if it isn't making sense

03:58.569 --> 04:01.345
and even as you get more
and more familiar with this,

04:01.345 --> 04:02.897
I encourage you to try out the numbers.

04:02.897 --> 04:05.427
That will give you more,
instead of just memorizing,

04:05.427 --> 04:07.103
hey, if I shift to the right,

04:07.103 --> 04:10.335
I replace x with x minus
the amount that I shift.

04:10.335 --> 04:12.340
Always try out the numbers
and try to get an intuition

04:12.340 --> 04:15.078
for that why that works.

04:15.078 --> 04:18.588
But now, let's start from
here and shift four up

04:18.588 --> 04:22.708
and shifting four up is in
some ways a lot more intuitive.

04:22.708 --> 04:24.208
So let me do that.

04:25.322 --> 04:27.072
Let me shift four up.

04:29.485 --> 04:31.485
Alright, so let me move.

04:33.286 --> 04:36.703
I'm gonna go up one, two, three and four.

04:39.501 --> 04:41.180
I think I got that right.

04:41.180 --> 04:44.340
So now I've shifted four up.

04:44.340 --> 04:46.975
And just as a reminder
of what we've even done,

04:46.975 --> 04:50.642
the first part we shifted
three to the right

04:51.508 --> 04:54.175
and now we are shifting four up.

04:55.553 --> 04:58.553
So now, now we are shifting four up.

05:01.313 --> 05:03.813
So before, y equaled zero here

05:05.068 --> 05:07.886
but now, y needs to be equal to four.

05:07.886 --> 05:09.552
So whatever this was evaluating,

05:09.552 --> 05:11.886
do we now have to add four to it?

05:11.886 --> 05:14.015
So when we just shifted
three to the right,

05:14.015 --> 05:17.123
our equation was y is
equal to the absolute value

05:17.123 --> 05:19.085
of x minus three

05:19.085 --> 05:20.847
but now whatever we were getting before,

05:20.847 --> 05:22.279
we now have to add four to it.

05:22.279 --> 05:25.386
We're going up in the vertical direction.

05:25.386 --> 05:27.719
So we just have to add four.

05:28.862 --> 05:30.659
Now, this makes a little bit more sense.

05:30.659 --> 05:33.720
If you're shifting in
the vertical direction,

05:33.720 --> 05:35.598
if you shift up in the vertical direction,

05:35.598 --> 05:38.828
well, you just add a constant
by the amount you're shifting.

05:38.828 --> 05:40.908
If you shift down in
the vertical direction,

05:40.908 --> 05:41.894
well, you would subtract.

05:41.894 --> 05:43.451
If we said shift down four,

05:43.451 --> 05:46.027
you would subtract four right over here.

05:46.027 --> 05:48.444
The less intuitive thing
is what we did with x

05:48.444 --> 05:50.205
'cause when you shift to the right,

05:50.205 --> 05:52.090
you actually replace your x

05:52.090 --> 05:55.174
with x minus the amount that you shifted

05:55.174 --> 05:57.197
but once again, try out numbers

05:57.197 --> 06:00.631
until it really makes some
intuitive sense for you

06:00.631 --> 06:02.636
but this is what we would finally get.

06:02.636 --> 06:05.583
The equation of this thing right over here

06:05.583 --> 06:07.997
is y is equal to the absolute value of x

06:07.997 --> 06:09.830
minus three plus four.
